[{"id":"VRCE-6-99-1","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":99,"verse":1,"english":"The foremost of the wives of the Rākşasas (king) bewailing piteously cast her looks poorly towards her husband. And beholding her Tennecked husband slain by Rāma of Inconceivable actions Mandodarī bewailed there piteously.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.754,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-111-1"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6099001","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"168e3465406697305b9dfcddd55f2a9aa4360a3d9a7b71b5281e7f550c8a0632","compact":"72d1d4fc1c99511d979fc642946e775003df3eb93bee0a8ff516d35e4b6a7df6","nasal":"72d1d4fc1c99511d979fc642946e775003df3eb93bee0a8ff516d35e4b6a7df6"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-99-2","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":99,"verse":2,"english":"The foremost of the wives of the Rākşasas (king) bewailing piteously cast her looks poorly towards her husband. And beholding her Tennecked husband slain by Rāma of Inconceivable actions Mandodarī bewailed there piteously.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.839,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-111-1"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6099002","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"77cca2d67e3208fae6e04bc444f8eb1100a2e95c77a7de477f62328a5de60b7b","compact":"f5bc9910487e8a2a0e2ef51c9581d45e6fae1db3fcc9897bd3a7f941ab474083","nasal":"66b1cdb120b7d6561322197a68f6e7ca84e24a8d2482bd301cbdcf4aaf77c73f"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-99-3","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":99,"verse":3,"english":"O you of huge arms! O younger brother of Baishravana! Even Purandara feared to stand before you when enraged.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-111-2"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6099003","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"bcd307a83b96cd542980a7306ad5b78c8ca4f56ec0ed100df93566997c8983c5","compact":"94659bce4820975019ca3a01e8220d89e155ff271d3c920ebcb3b82636c6ee6f","nasal":"94659bce4820975019ca3a01e8220d89e155ff271d3c920ebcb3b82636c6ee6f"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-99-4","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":99,"verse":4,"english":"The great Rşis-the far-famed Gandharvas and the charanas, fled away to different quarters in your fear.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.793,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-111-3"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6099004","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"534f88ba6775b8d090e70e3111bbeff11dea311922515b316dff9e9fbe399f74","compact":"d1d47eb1ed868f394790a4186b1ffda856e4781cb36c358da4f8b8d136285e4c","nasal":"53503489dfaabc529bd32cf86e60afc79045b08681e102e0a42737108442c11c"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-99-5","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":99,"verse":5,"english":"Then (how) have you been overpowered in battle by Rāma who is a mere man? Why is it that you are not ashamed of it, О king, O lord of the Raksasas?","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.932,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-111-4"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6099005","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"c5796363e93f2042d5a7ac27e6ba2460e636020273b9004aee1ac1874004bd17","compact":"9aaf3ae40f0ffd57d3dc9b40244183eaebfad97c75eb86a0e97ab44498040078","nasal":"9aaf3ae40f0ffd57d3dc9b40244183eaebfad97c75eb86a0e97ab44498040078"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-99-6","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":99,"verse":6,"english":"Conquering the three worlds with your prowess you did attain your glory; and it is unbearable, that a man, ranging in the forest, has slain you.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-111-5"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6099006","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"109def6e6a85c950a312f8ed3bfd7ebd9b0703b8b2593126d82696d932278680","compact":"bf83be5ec4200f391dd4db5b470e9da37821b8574021089496eb9926f6e5cc9d","nasal":"bf83be5ec4200f391dd4db5b470e9da37821b8574021089496eb9926f6e5cc9d"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-99-7","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":99,"verse":7,"english":"You who are capable of assuming shapes at will have been slain in conflict by Rāma, in the city of Lankā unapproachable by men.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-111-6"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6099007","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"1583f5ede9df9174ba55d11ccbbaa09b24a23b1b7b8f2b8c07754d239ddf6d26","compact":"1ec46f7ee2cae0f368114b8c4ba13c1657c3913c7e42e6a4a946504ae52f5e20","nasal":"1ec46f7ee2cae0f368114b8c4ba13c1657c3913c7e42e6a4a946504ae52f5e20"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-99-8","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":99,"verse":8,"english":"I do not believe that your destruction, who had always been crowned with success, before the forces, is work of Rāma.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.875,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-111-7"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6099008","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"da87bbd5e412da1853cbc4e395efeabd567016e7f89e62bbfc54d5bd8b9c2585","compact":"e0ef5537e9752f8d495cdf8d2934e6c9c942e7e0c2f5de254ea6b39edd13bdf9","nasal":"e0ef5537e9752f8d495cdf8d2934e6c9c942e7e0c2f5de254ea6b39edd13bdf9"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-99-9","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":99,"verse":9,"english":"Subduing all your passions, you did conquer the three worlds-remembering their grudge they have now over powered you.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.886,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-111-11"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6099009","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"b9e63aa3a7456ca5146924ccd4ff7204a61d13492d6102e3dfd8b9ea81150154","compact":"1b83a309ea29e60683678c702cb7ef7f10d9544b3b7a4834357ddd8a9b538ed1","nasal":"31c5371ff2ed07e364470bd8a9d29c9aac2a337119667beb6753a8579bd5816f"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-99-10","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":99,"verse":10,"english":"(Methinks) Death (himself) came there in the shape of Rāma and spread illusions unconsciously for your destruction, O you of great strength.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.792,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-111-8"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6099010","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"93dfc5b58a37558bf992ee3d459a46163fd502636df034fd692b3c2d580bd894","compact":"c4084c6c2e753e77f800dfa91a883f1b0189dec268e71bfb08ccc7889f24990a","nasal":"c4084c6c2e753e77f800dfa91a883f1b0189dec268e71bfb08ccc7889f24990a"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-99-11","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":99,"verse":11,"english":"Rāma is not a man since he slew at Janasthāna your brother Khara encircied by many a Rāks asas.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.643,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-111-12"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6099011","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"e9abef0dcdca16d8a66942f1504defa36aded7b4cf3a9fd662c942f55c9ad5b8","compact":"d0e07add8963facfeac48fc6e6d298a7ac3150bfc0de0c015e983de7204251b2","nasal":"d0e07add8963facfeac48fc6e6d298a7ac3150bfc0de0c015e983de7204251b2"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-99-12","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":99,"verse":12,"english":"We were sore-distressed when Hanuman, by his own prowess, entered the city of Lanka incapable of being approached even by the celestials.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.667,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-111-13"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6099012","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"e33c5b2143bb0ac1d243d40f826734de1fba966b34c220bc06b54e9b1063e1b9","compact":"05d40c704271aeaa1c88057003f1b2e717a41b655b80564d0e0e664b23e2754d","nasal":"642cf70735b3c4568a4b8ea7e9df84b0170e739be6d5a0bdf272dd78760668a5"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-99-13","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":99,"verse":13,"english":"I prevented you from creating enmity with Rāghava but you did not pay heed to my words and this is the result (thereof).","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.869,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-111-14"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6099013","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"33b50272a57757b2b1f182cd5205845c066a62a1e5afe99f94858e1d08cd2146","compact":"f42179c7fccc4d500aba4cac603e8ea59367eff443b97a8dcfa341583aa94de2","nasal":"f42179c7fccc4d500aba4cac603e8ea59367eff443b97a8dcfa341583aa94de2"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-99-14","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":99,"verse":14,"english":"O foremost of Rākşasas-0 you of a vicious understanding, for the destruction of your wealth yourself and your relatives, you did suddenly cherish amour for Sitā, greater than-Yeven) Arundhati and Rohiņi. Forsooth you did perpetrated an unbecoming deed by distressing the adorable Sitā ever devoted to her lord, an earth* even to Earth herself and a Śrī (Śrt is the goddess of wealth and good fortune-but Sitā is more fortunate than fortune herself-) even to Śrī herself. *The Earth is an emblem of patience but Sítā is more patient than the earth.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.864,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-111-15"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6099014","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"b38b3061999d0cf14bed79ac75e2081abb767528b20f996a72e588c6630f80d7","compact":"44f091cd6088c5db0a471783809f538ea08549cc7bb7f800c09df851095c5133","nasal":"44f091cd6088c5db0a471783809f538ea08549cc7bb7f800c09df851095c5133"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-99-15","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":99,"verse":15,"english":"O foremost of Rākşasas-0 you of a vicious understanding, for the destruction of your wealth yourself and your relatives, you did suddenly cherish amour for Sitā, greater than-Yeven) Arundhati and Rohiņi. Forsooth you did perpetrated an unbecoming deed by distressing the adorable Sitā ever devoted to her lord, an earth* even to Earth herself and a Śrī (Śrt is the goddess of wealth and good fortune-but Sitā is more fortunate than fortune herself-) even to Śrī herself. *The Earth is an emblem of patience but Sítā is more patient than the earth.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.904,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-111-15"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6099015","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"d3448e33b51472f1eb95a910185cbe5c3481b8da96e35e78e5225387415abf3b","compact":"60b81c673c4c9fea47ae4c56382832a9622972a1324b171c17f75d88864f74d7","nasal":"75422595fb12a81fb688a666d4c048c6da5ec86822eeaadd151157dd5c182931"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-99-16","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":99,"verse":16,"english":"Maithili is not my equal nor superior either in birth, beauty or accomplishments, but you did not perceive this by your misgivings.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.683,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-111-21"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6099016","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"b3a1ecc822089fd51c4de9e177291205ce1b4d64a6bfede71f9d8bb61ac05800","compact":"7772720cfcf3a1298a9715ce85e13c6b4319b6cb564b3a9cd06ef34fbd829ec0","nasal":"b872bcaf09579d7436e2496990e01a1518d98bfc7f4c0593d1e1e26474958c93"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-99-17","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":99,"verse":17,"english":"Death does not always visit all men without any cause-and Maithili is the cause of the death.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.633,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-111-22"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6099017","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"d32a4bc2832334eea5d6e3f3a5fa33843e4ab87ab23b00524f55dc3664b92eeb","compact":"fca43cc3edf5dd7b97c2c88881b0d4037f3d46c0460ea93d500f694d9199dca9","nasal":"fca43cc3edf5dd7b97c2c88881b0d4037f3d46c0460ea93d500f694d9199dca9"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-99-18","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":99,"verse":18,"english":"And death, in consequence of Maithili, has taken you far away. And she, shorn of all sorrow, shall enjoy in the company of Rāma, and I, of limited piety, am now sunk in the ocean of grief.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-111-23"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6099018","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"2b2c585310de03759bb4fa1f2efe6c472260b8a6dfebdfff7a2887c0130de905","compact":"a8d2f5e8b5efd81223f5a82913bb03debe9dd8e62b6b2b3f8e4148b7b08a03ae","nasal":"a8d2f5e8b5efd81223f5a82913bb03debe9dd8e62b6b2b3f8e4148b7b08a03ae"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-99-19","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":99,"verse":19,"english":"Roaming at large with you in a car unequalled in beauty on the hill Kailāsa Mandara, Meru, in the garden of Caitraratha and all other celestial gardens, beholding many a country, wearing variegated clothes and garlands, I have been deprived of all pleasures and enjoyments, O hero, by your death.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-111-24"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6099019","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"82d533839e672f74db8fa67fdc3c360289261fa65e8c9072166c10e5dee89425","compact":"b2e9d9af7608f50378c1ba2cdcaa400f2ad472e3796cb9ad1e96090ef915ba3f","nasal":"7a32e1b0be6bfcaa072aae0d5bdb34c666dbab210c2c564b1cd0187e30a89e34"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-99-20","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":99,"verse":20,"english":"Roaming at large with you in a car unequalled in beauty on the hill Kailāsa Mandara, Meru, in the garden of Caitraratha and all other celestial gardens, beholding many a country, wearing variegated clothes and garlands, I have been deprived of all pleasures and enjoyments, O hero, by your death.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.907,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-111-24"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6099020","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"bf330599fd9b51f9db7fb70cad28b09cf91de57ba884246d8e221281e47fa45a","compact":"44e6b1a64b7783ce8be17dccd56d486b9bb8399f35bce6b09cf79200c6248d85","nasal":"eb4371ac1fc838aad34b21a13009992954c7234c95a7b66db0199aa3c1cd009e"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-99-21","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":99,"verse":21,"english":"Beholding the daughter of the king of Mithila brought (in the city of Lanka) what, your younger brother Vibhīşaņa, thinking and sighing, said has now proved true, O you of long-arms.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.705,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-111-44"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6099021","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"fd2c3154a1b0add2e41c3b03fabfaf87a44ebd90fb91bbf0507007896aece613","compact":"1ba61024956c588e0bcaaa8dfea7452e6636c7a533fc3a9b8a9c3d068c048d6e","nasal":"1ba61024956c588e0bcaaa8dfea7452e6636c7a533fc3a9b8a9c3d068c048d6e"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-99-22","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":99,"verse":22,"english":"This destruction of the leading Rākṣasas has proceeded from the disaster arising from your anger and lust. For your (vicious) deeds all our good fortune is lost-(and from them) has proceeded the great disaster exterminating the race. And by you all the Raksasa families have been deprived of their lords.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.695,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-111-45"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6099022","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"7af175d096d0c7dd3515bc4e81eb2c4b5aabd6b5b8bc1bf35a9566c7de8c6ecc","compact":"d23945fe89cc9c7f85969236ee47d4b8d8830e93e66de86acccf47a83c8afeff","nasal":"e62df4a998bc364f79aa375eda2703a690e91376211e3343ceaad522833c6b8a"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-99-23","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":99,"verse":23,"english":"You well-known for your strength and manliness, are not worthy of being grieved by me. On account of my effeminate nature my understanding is possessed by sorrow.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-111-46"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6099023","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"f8b8b6d1a146a709ce6ce842efe6c5a9131d478c5fdcfe73a43dc22762abc331","compact":"7047116707bd344d55437e4e4e3cd06035ea67b84d55d8f45f2b875577ba43fe","nasal":"7047116707bd344d55437e4e4e3cd06035ea67b84d55d8f45f2b875577ba43fe"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-99-24","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":99,"verse":24,"english":"Carrying your pious and iniquitous deeds you have attained to your own state-I am only lamenting for me who have been sorry for your destruction.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.853,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-111-47"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6099024","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"0e722e783760352f4d15ee109c33202bd94e26de8c8a4b1040b6b82392f91c5c","compact":"e137427591d69501bd65f21abc08b6847bd97a4b7ad6bddadc574976b82d484d","nasal":"e137427591d69501bd65f21abc08b6847bd97a4b7ad6bddadc574976b82d484d"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-99-25","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":99,"verse":25,"english":"O you resembling the red clouds O you wearing yellow cloth and excellent Angada, stretching your person on the ground why are you in the long run bathed in blood? Why did you not like one asleep welcome me who am stricken with grief?","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.53,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-111-51"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6099025","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"6faea76f79efe84105f0041cc6effd050d1dcf37692b6ccec923d82c6b542392","compact":"a63210a7fdef387e2ae2363d79029c3a054d17b957497308f90339e8aaf29682","nasal":"3ce8e7429b065e4a1c45480efbbce4648d22b8ed0f2d9545d9c731c3e88850eb"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-99-26","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":99,"verse":26,"english":"I am the grand-daughter of the highly powerful Rākşasa Sumālī who never flies away from the field of battle; why did you not welcome me.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.594,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-111-52"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6099026","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"075107aca09884664481bf2c4a37fe79983f7eb6b72d81f6473f8297f1c85095","compact":"b3e47e98a05b93a514646f89dccd03fe4761e0ece0e7cc61987ee722d471557c","nasal":"b3e47e98a05b93a514646f89dccd03fe4761e0ece0e7cc61987ee722d471557c"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-99-27","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":99,"verse":27,"english":"Rise up! rise up! why did you lie down (on this occasion of) new discomfiture? Today have the rays of the Sun entered fearlessly the city of Lanka. The parigha, by which, brilliant as the rays of the Sun, you did distress the enemies in conflict which was always adored by you like the thunder of the wielder of thunder-bolt, which slew many in battle, and which was adorned with golden nets now Leith shattered into thousand pieces by arrows.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.857,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-111-53"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6099027","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"de5a600a8547bf3a9951031f8106d9e53b585949b9c799bef8646d7b26ba2a1d","compact":"b5a3fc4c0957d8f5ddab9b0c41dfa42ba6a73be44f68a6962e2649d1b93825c5","nasal":"b5a3fc4c0957d8f5ddab9b0c41dfa42ba6a73be44f68a6962e2649d1b93825c5"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-99-28","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":99,"verse":28,"english":"Rise up! rise up! why did you lie down (on this occasion of) new discomfiture? Today have the rays of the Sun entered fearlessly the city of Lanka. The parigha, by which, brilliant as the rays of the Sun, you did distress the enemies in conflict which was always adored by you like the thunder of the wielder of thunder-bolt, which slew many in battle, and which was adorned with golden nets now Leith shattered into thousand pieces by arrows.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.883,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-111-53"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6099028","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"f325fe83befcf17f6d058e22c823507731adeb1eddeb387275448299ad292288","compact":"fb7a93375794e844edaceee23ee20342a6e7a9904328ec5924d02d196cb2aabc","nasal":"8fa5d69af359789716f4cc0c4b388488192982943d5c94a4862e5d3915c05d0e"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-99-29","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":99,"verse":29,"english":"Why did you lie on the battle-field embracing her like your beloved spouse? Why did you not wish tr welcome me like one not beloved to you? Ok fie on this heart of mine which is not sundered into thousand (pieces) albeit distressed with the grief of your death!","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.875,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-111-54"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6099029","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"92e3552969cfcf32528f2164242906f791f6fcca7c314513928f7d5af09b0a0d","compact":"7c5f3313ea828b0b2eee8d2e5d5bbb38d8031ba3d353cb7fce7d5ec81dc92f25","nasal":"c4e0aceeaa74c00210048a3ca3d64a987c4f4e63828a575e15f414b7f14fab35"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-99-30","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":99,"verse":30,"english":"In the meantime Rama said to Vibhrsana, “Do you perform the funeral ceremonies of your brother and console his wives.\"","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.773,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-111-59"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6099030","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"0800da3723b7ae4ddd92e522947b3da727e21e05679f6d1df44e49320f860f75","compact":"07cc81e184ffe4588b03dca93c627ce7ace0dd67c803048057eb7e09d5b89ada","nasal":"71c593a145846c0a684e67d03308926f72cb0e387005290cbae2ea2a2666c378"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-99-31","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":99,"verse":31,"english":"Where to the intelligent Vibhīşaņa replied with the following words-pointing out wealth and Piety, and judging by his understanding what is proper.","alignment":{"type":"approximate","confidence":0.15,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-111-60"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6099031","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"830096b2a1837dd98a36ee645fbe695c52ec575954926e65a71eed497bde7ada","compact":"146bb683ea999a585a4121528904c6445d56b9f744778cc3e404abd47d7d7f2b","nasal":"146bb683ea999a585a4121528904c6445d56b9f744778cc3e404abd47d7d7f2b"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-99-32","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":99,"verse":32,"english":"\"I do not think it proper to perform his cremation ceremony who had renounced all pious deeds was wicked cruel, liar and who had ravished others' wives.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.688,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-111-61"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6099032","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"a1853700e556e7b8a5e13aeb4bb62af40ff541dc9c15bd061790bedf5de5d555","compact":"ebfb549d6fdc031759c6180d42b513a2564f5b66ab522cb113cae3d3d6ce0970","nasal":"ebfb549d6fdc031759c6180d42b513a2564f5b66ab522cb113cae3d3d6ce0970"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-99-33","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":99,"verse":33,"english":"He is my enemy in the shape of a brother ever engaged in doing injury to others and Rāvana is not worthy of my adoration albeit he is adorable by virtue of his being my elder brother.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.857,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-111-62"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6099033","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"e0088da1048aba78853bf102e7681e54a5b703ccfa57fbad32ab34355030cc20","compact":"5201d34c169b3e41da845142a9f31de468693df561ad56b794aa4524fe5e7f03","nasal":"5201d34c169b3e41da845142a9f31de468693df561ad56b794aa4524fe5e7f03"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-99-34","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":99,"verse":34,"english":"O Rāma, perhaps people of this earth will call me cruel but they will again recognise my act as good when they will hear of his vicious deeds.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.899,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-111-63"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6099034","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"f704d9a8e3ee070d916246f4b32c9e09d4d4ea6987df5fff5ec3ffe191444d8c","compact":"2b38dcb1737f95cc75b7cbb95fe4105ee4b0b83d34017e8f98d5c46e75286aa5","nasal":"3776914f4e8c006fb67dc2416d394319094ee572e526cff7bbb183df3981ceb8"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-99-35","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":99,"verse":35,"english":"Hearing those words, Rāma, the foremost of the pious and conversant with the skill of speech greatly delighted, spoke to Vibhisana (equally) skilled in speech.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.844,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-111-64"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6099035","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"a3839d7a42a03ebb9672ad0c8a9603e7899c2d01bd0afcd90bf43f306137e41b","compact":"2e8b54dd43f29dd17fa0c571ef157f4a9c1fe09ff0f9b3b7be4727ac5b495bff","nasal":"2e8b54dd43f29dd17fa0c571ef157f4a9c1fe09ff0f9b3b7be4727ac5b495bff"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-99-36","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":99,"verse":36,"english":"It behove me to encompass your welfare since by your help I have gained the victory. I lord of Räkșasas, forsooth, you should hear my wellmeaning words.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.729,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-111-65"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6099036","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"bf7e36e1041b01fedd5551b0b6a0963d2f502a39806de366cbf292247f5ae88f","compact":"a28c2146ebb37bb87ccc87824ad4ee3498c01cba6c11e211c59f13fea691785c","nasal":"a28c2146ebb37bb87ccc87824ad4ee3498c01cba6c11e211c59f13fea691785c"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-99-37","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":99,"verse":37,"english":"Although this night-ranger perpetrated many vicious and impious deeds still he was ever powerful, heroic and strong in warfare.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.724,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-111-66"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6099037","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"e38b338f66ab3a54418d9c0a6bbb6edf652c1b419133ea78211b99d9671f64cb","compact":"4c1fc0def23c39ebea2a155d7e58412bd0612068e62980c76eb0c32c6c1d25e3","nasal":"4c1fc0def23c39ebea2a155d7e58412bd0612068e62980c76eb0c32c6c1d25e3"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-99-38","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":99,"verse":38,"english":"I have heard that this high-souled Ravana, gifted with strength and a dread to all people was not defeated (even) by the celestials headed by the performer of hundred sacrifices.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.873,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-111-67"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6099038","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"43caa3cd691947678145d896d07f766ab60980cc7a0b87cd594ed183a7b277f0","compact":"1d38524bd4911d37333e251c6b05085ea6c18d18a515eb70b1e1660f172a4bd2","nasal":"7127863b5e9e761adf9a8c964cc5858e11b8603246f95d1f2751876a43b7d453"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-99-39","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":99,"verse":39,"english":"Enmity extend up to death-so it has ended; there is no necessity (of carrying it on). Do you (therefore) perform his cremation ceremony-he is to you as he is to me.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.806,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-111-68"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6099039","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"1092957f6a5426fc00d3f7e0494fe49916b6348f019593fa43654132b45fee32","compact":"458a1e33bc69573c840e4764f4205ccb8696873eeb896062b6928b82756ffece","nasal":"f4729bf296d4fc229c671deffd4023f0d8056f0c81f55e06a3fabda828332b2d"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-99-40","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":99,"verse":40,"english":"O you of long-arms it behove the to perform speedily with due rites and religious ceremonies his funeral ceremony-you shall be the object of praise (to people).","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.859,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-111-69"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6099040","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"10641565014f152adfb3e9249784deb3fd57946058690115d6d6a0cd092a5fe8","compact":"69c1c3f93a4e4333da98d088cbe523966ca2f64f4837f6b7c620461843a3ca61","nasal":"69c1c3f93a4e4333da98d088cbe523966ca2f64f4837f6b7c620461843a3ca61"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-99-41","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":99,"verse":41,"english":"Hearing the words of Rāghava, Vibhīşaņa hastened on and began to make arrangements for the cremation of his slain brother Råvana.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.579,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-111-70"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6099041","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"ca2aae0d0edd76abc9aeeee889228ea2e65d513b3622d9897e6eec7b1debd7e9","compact":"f6983eceb05ae32a7d04fc856aaf1428717c8f1b22f742788652f38bf9265e51","nasal":"f6983eceb05ae32a7d04fc856aaf1428717c8f1b22f742788652f38bf9265e51"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-99-42","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":99,"verse":42,"english":"Vibhīşaņa according to due rites put fire to his (funeral pyre). Bathing and with wetted cloth, offering duly linseed and sacrificial grass mixed with water and consoling (Ravana's) wives again and again, he entreated them to go back.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.723,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-111-80"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6099042","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"19b4ededcb04204aa4fbd3ead1b2741310a3bcec89ca99e3d9fee096979c503c","compact":"279fa99a7b5eae0a5a0e975e274caa53f198a70c91265b5f6774829eed628840","nasal":"a9ed056a173fb51c590f2f87fd0b6164895b09cb3fd77ed54b993778343f00d3"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-99-43","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":99,"verse":43,"english":"They then entered the city. And those damsels having entered the city, Vibhisana, the lord of Rākşasas, approaching Rāma, stood by his side gently.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.469,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-111-81"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6099043","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"b71dd618a167671920eeba32ab2f04c196e494490c6587cc1f9a7af40fb9f4bd","compact":"ace08474eb4e7a432d46830c6ef2d2d6a944be5d579f910bfe4dc400558cdc5b","nasal":"ace08474eb4e7a432d46830c6ef2d2d6a944be5d579f910bfe4dc400558cdc5b"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-99-44","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":99,"verse":44,"english":"Rāma too, along with his army, Sugrīva and Lakşmana, was greatly delighted after slaying (the demon) Vitra.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.597,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-111-82"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6099044","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"6c0ca726165c21cc8155d075a89f760e110d8307778676252a36e4723883711d","compact":"2640bc5adaac3102bfb40878ebee3f1967cb6da1e3a203ab872f92679168a742","nasal":"2640bc5adaac3102bfb40878ebee3f1967cb6da1e3a203ab872f92679168a742"}}]
